CRead Disk 1
name=HELLO
api=1
about=A sample diskette - copy it and write your own
author=cread

---FILE README.TXT
This is a data diskette: plain text, no code.

Drop a .DSK file into the Disks folder inside your vault and it appears on the
boot screen the next time you land there.

A small game or a mail reader would be a program disk instead: same container,
with the payload being bytecode rather than text. That is the next step.

---FILE FORMAT.TXT
Line 1 has to be:   CRead Disk 1

Then key=value lines until the first file:

  name      the label on the drive list (required)
  api       container version, currently 1
  about     one line of description
  author    who made it

Every file starts with a line:

  ---FILE NAME.TXT

...and runs until the next ---FILE line. Everything is plain UTF-8 text, so a
diskette can be read with `type`, mailed around or put in git.
